error: `nint` has the size of an address, which depends on the machine; a number kept in bytes has a size of its own
  --> error_endian_to_size_of_address.sg:3:26
 3 |     print(bytes.length().toLittleEndian())
   |                          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  hint: make it a `long` first: `((long)bytes.length()).toLittleEndian()` gives 8 bytes
